[ti:One Player Too Many]
[ar:mippithedork]
[offset:0]

[00:00.00]Come on in, kid. Pull you up a chair. I hear you're makin' yourself a video game.
[00:08.00]That's wonderful.
[00:10.00]Now tell me somethin'...
[00:13.00]You ain't plannin' on makin' it multiplayer, are ya?
[00:19.00]You say, Well, actually...
[00:22.00]Oh, Lord.
[00:26.00]I knew a boy from Tennessee
[00:29.00]Made a platformer, just like me
[00:32.00]Had a little jump, had a little dash
[00:35.00]Had a little dream of makin' cash
[00:38.00]Then one fine day, his buddy said
[00:41.00]"Let's put two players in instead!"
[00:43.00]Now his jump don't jump, his dash don't dash
[00:46.00]And his server bill's eatin' all his cash
[00:49.00]One player jumps, and all is fine
[00:52.00]Two players jump, you bend space-time
[00:55.00]Three players join, the world's on fire
[00:58.00]Four players crash the whole damn wire!
[01:01.00]Don't put multiplayer in that game, son!
[01:03.00]Don't go thinkin' it'll be more fun!
[01:06.00]You got one little player, and he works just fine
[01:09.00]Now you wanna synchronize him 'cross space 'n time?
[01:12.00]You'll lose your sleep, you'll lose your hair
[01:15.00]You'll debug ghosts that ain't even there
[01:18.00]You can make that game, you can get it done
[01:21.00]Just don't put multiplayer in that game, son!
[01:27.00]I knew a gal with a racing game
[01:30.00]Single-player, smooth as a Cadillac frame
[01:33.00]Then she added online play
[01:35.00]And watched the cars just float away
[01:38.00]One car's here, one car's there
[01:40.00]One's upside down and one ain't anywhere
[01:43.00]She said "I'll fix it with interpolation"
[01:46.00]Now they're driftin' through the fourth dimension!
[01:49.00]You say... But what about rollback?
[01:51.00]Oh, honey...
[01:55.00]I knew a team with a sword and shield
[01:58.00]Built a hundred monsters in a field
[02:01.00]Then someone said "Let's play with friends!"
[02:03.00]That's where the happy story ends
[02:06.00]Now who gets loot? And who gets gold?
[02:09.00]Who owns the quest when the host gets old?
[02:11.00]Who's in charge when the players split?
[02:14.00]And why's that goblin attacking itself?!
[02:17.00]The client says hit! The server says miss!
[02:20.00]The player's screaming "WHAT THE HELL IS THIS?"
[02:22.00]He swears he dodged, the logs disagree
[02:25.00]And somebody's duplicated the currency!
[02:28.00]Don't put multiplayer in that game, son!
[02:30.00]Don't go thinkin' it'll be more fun!
[02:33.00]You got one little player, and he works just fine
[02:36.00]Now you wanna synchronize him 'cross space 'n time?
[02:39.00]You'll lose your sleep, you'll lose your hair
[02:42.00]You'll debug ghosts that ain't even there
[02:44.00]You can make that game, you can get it done
[02:47.00]Just don't put multiplayer in that game, son!
[02:52.00]Now listen close, I'll tell you true
[02:55.00]Multiplayer ain't just player two
[02:58.00]It's servers, bandwidth, fraud, and fees
[03:01.00]And players spread across seven seas
[03:03.00]It's lobbies, parties, matchmaking queues
[03:06.00]It's disconnects and the rage-quit blues
[03:09.00]It's balancing powers for four or five
[03:11.00]And keeping an empty world alive
[03:14.00]And that's before somebody figures out how to cheat.
[03:17.00]But you say, I just want my friends to play together!
[03:20.00]So did the last twelve studios I buried...
[03:35.00]I knew a man, he made a farm
[03:38.00]Had little chickens, had a great big barn
[03:41.00]He said "My wife could join me too!"
[03:43.00]Next thing you know, there's a chicken coup!
[03:46.00]The eggs got duped, the cows desynced
[03:49.00]The crops rolled back, the database blinked
[03:52.00]His wife logged out, the world went black
[03:54.00]His chickens traveled three days back!
[03:57.00]Now he's got servers coast to coast
[04:00.00]A million chickens and a missing host
[04:03.00]And every time somebody plants a seed
[04:05.00]His backend starts to smoke and bleed!
[04:08.00]DON'T PUT MULTIPLAYER IN THAT GAME, SON!
[04:10.00]DON'T GO THINKIN' IT'LL BE MORE FUN!
[04:13.00]You got one little player, and he works just fine
[04:16.00]Now you wanna synchronize him 'cross space 'n time?
[04:19.00]You'll lose your sleep, you'll lose your hair
[04:22.00]You'll debug ghosts that ain't even there
[04:24.00]You can make that game, you can get it done
[04:27.00]JUST DON'T PUT MULTIPLAYER IN THAT GAME, SON!
[04:32.00]Now, I ain't sayin' multiplayer games ain't worth makin'.
[04:37.00]Some of the finest games ever made were multiplayer.
[04:41.00]I'm just sayin'...
[04:43.00]If you ain't ever made a game before, maybe don't start with the kind that needs four computers to agree on where a chicken is.
[04:51.00]Okay, but what if it's an MMO?
[04:55.00]...Get out.
